# Words of ours for US English's root volume: a word here is written in small
# letters and is found whatever its capitals, and inside a longer word as a
# stem, so one entry gives its plural and its possessive too. What is said in
# its place has to be one word or a phonetic spelling; several words do
# nothing here, and go in main.dic instead. One a line, the word, a tab, and
# what is said; tools/module/builtindict.py reads it after the community's,
# so an entry here replaces theirs.

